    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Microsoft is a public company founded in 1975 and headquartered in Redmond, Washington. Its Power Automate product page describes workflow and business process automation across apps, systems, and websites using AI, digital, and robotic process automation. The page says Power Automate can automate across nearly unlimited systems, desktop apps, and websites, and includes quotes stating that generative AI and Power Automate reduced a data validation process from over 100 people to a few people, and that Power Automate provides leading generative AI and process mining capabilities within the Power Platform ecosystem.\n\nMicrosoft's AI portfolio includes Microsoft Copilot, embedded across M365, Azure OpenAI Service, Azure Machine Learning, AutoGen (Microsoft), Semantic Kernel, Microsoft Agent Framework, Microsoft Designer, Microsoft Teams AI, SharePoint AI, Microsoft Clipchamp AI, and Microsoft Power Automate AI. Azure OpenAI Service provides OpenAI models in Azure regions with enterprise content filtering, Entra ID integration, and data residency controls. Azure Machine Learning is an MLOps platform with AutoML, model registry, and responsible AI toolkit integration. AutoGen (Microsoft) is a multi-agent conversation framework from Microsoft Research. Semantic Kernel is a model-agnostic orchestration SDK for .NET, Python, and Java, superseded by Microsoft Agent Framework in 2026. Microsoft Agent Framework is a unified .NET and Python agent SDK with graph workflows and native MCP and A2A support. Microsoft Power Automate AI is described as enterprise workflow automation with Copilot integration, M365 data access, and DLP integration.\n\nMicrosoft reported revenue of $331,839,000,000 for the fiscal year ended June 30, 2026 in a Form 10-K, and trades under ticker MSFT with CIK 0000789019. Litigation records include The New York Times Co. v. Microsoft Corp. and OpenAI and Authors Guild v. OpenAI, Inc., both in the U.S. District Court for the Southern District of New York. Washington state records list 114 law exposure entries for Microsoft.",
